# ASCII-ONLY DOCTRINE - NO EXCEPTIONS

ALWAYS apply this rule. It is permanent.

- NEVER write emoji or pictographic symbols (smileys, hearts, stars, checkmarks, X marks, and similar)
- NEVER write Unicode arrow glyphs, box-drawing characters, or triangle / down-arrow symbols (use ASCII sequences such as `->`, `<->`, `v`, `down`)
- NEVER write curly quotes or em dash / en dash characters
- ALWAYS use ASCII (code points 32 through 126) only for normative text

Replacements:

- `[x]` or OK for checkmark
- `[ ]` or FAIL for X mark
- `->` for direction (arrow meaning)
- `--` for em dash
- Straight `"` and `'` for quotes

When editing existing files with mojibake (UTF-8 shown wrong after a bad encoding conversion, often shown as `a-hat` plus garbage), replace with ASCII equivalents.

Canonical full text: [AGENTS.md](../../AGENTS.md) section **ASCII-ONLY DOCTRINE (LILITH / constitutional)**.

This rule is constitutional. Violations will be rejected.
